00:31:53.500 --> 00:31:56.050
- The crew boat itself--
this 70-foot boat--

00:31:56.050 --> 00:31:58.316
is a micromanaged
system in and of itself.

00:31:58.316 --> 00:32:00.190
You've got the
administrator-- your coxswain.

00:32:00.190 --> 00:32:01.690
And then you've got
your powerhouse.

00:32:01.690 --> 00:32:04.720
You've got your stroke, who's
your leader of your powerhouse.

00:32:04.720 --> 00:32:06.640
And then you've got your
four and five seats,

00:32:06.640 --> 00:32:08.681
who are the peak of your boat.

00:32:08.681 --> 00:32:10.680
And then you've got your
bow, who kind of guides

00:32:10.680 --> 00:32:12.820
you along in the little
directions, left and right.

00:32:12.820 --> 00:32:16.150
And so together, you work as
a team to the common goal.

00:32:16.150 --> 00:32:21.580
- They learn incredible amounts
about leadership, teamwork,

00:32:21.580 --> 00:32:26.800
sportsmanship, and courage--
the willingness to take risks

00:32:26.800 --> 00:32:29.980
and push their abilities
beyond what they think they can

00:32:29.980 --> 00:32:30.840
achieve.

00:32:30.840 --> 00:32:34.330
- I've learned to push
myself during races

00:32:34.330 --> 00:32:38.320
and during practices so
hard, and commit myself

00:32:38.320 --> 00:32:41.530
to a certain goal
unequivocally in a way

00:32:41.530 --> 00:32:43.128
that I never had before.

00:32:43.128 --> 00:32:45.080
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:55.700
- The MIT I knew in
the 60s and early 70s

00:32:55.700 --> 00:32:57.350
had a proper
emphasis on athletics

00:32:57.350 --> 00:32:59.570
and a tremendous
diversity of sports,

00:32:59.570 --> 00:33:01.670
and really emphasized
participation.

00:33:01.670 --> 00:33:03.230
That part hasn't changed.

00:33:03.230 --> 00:33:05.480
But what's happened is there's
an even greater variety

00:33:05.480 --> 00:33:06.410
of sports today.

00:33:06.410 --> 00:33:08.180
- If MIT doesn't
have something--

00:33:08.180 --> 00:33:10.545
be it a club or
organization or sport--

00:33:10.545 --> 00:33:12.920
if two people want to do it,
they'll let you organize it,

00:33:12.920 --> 00:33:13.753
and you can have it.

00:33:13.753 --> 00:33:16.981
It's up to the individual,
but MIT will embrace that.

00:33:16.981 --> 00:33:18.980
- It always has been in
the past and always will

00:33:18.980 --> 00:33:20.340
be about opportunity for all.

00:33:20.340 --> 00:33:22.340
- One of the things that
I think is particularly

00:33:22.340 --> 00:33:25.130
striking about the
athletic program at MIT

00:33:25.130 --> 00:33:28.790
is the emphasis on
participation in sports,

00:33:28.790 --> 00:33:30.410
rather than spectator sports.

00:33:30.410 --> 00:33:32.480
You don't see the
whole campus coming out

00:33:32.480 --> 00:33:34.880
to watch the football game
on a Saturday afternoon,

00:33:34.880 --> 00:33:37.100
like you might plan on
some college campuses.

00:33:37.100 --> 00:33:38.960
But you do see an
incredible number

00:33:38.960 --> 00:33:41.030
