04:40:46.870 --> 04:40:50.610
SPEAKER: Graduates,
congratulations.

04:40:50.610 --> 04:40:52.380
It's now my pleasure
to introduce

04:40:52.380 --> 04:40:58.620
Linda Sharpe, the Chief Marshal
who will greet the graduates.

04:40:58.620 --> 04:41:02.730
Miss Sharpe is a member
of the class of 1969

04:41:02.730 --> 04:41:05.719
and is currently serving as the
president of the Association

04:41:05.719 --> 04:41:08.572
of Alumni and Alumnae of MIT--

04:41:08.572 --> 04:41:09.072
Linda.

04:41:16.750 --> 04:41:21.010
SHARPE: It is my honor to
recognize the distinguished

04:41:21.010 --> 04:41:26.502
class of 2005, the
newest alumni of MIT.

04:41:26.502 --> 04:41:27.966
The entire--

04:41:27.966 --> 04:41:30.406
[CHEERING]

04:41:39.680 --> 04:41:48.020
The entire alumni body, now,
some 110,000-strong joins me

04:41:48.020 --> 04:41:54.200
in congratulating all of the
2005 graduates and officially

04:41:54.200 --> 04:41:57.380
welcoming you into
the alumni family,

04:41:57.380 --> 04:42:00.796
your infinite connection to MIT.

04:42:00.796 --> 04:42:03.236
[APPLAUSE]

04:42:14.000 --> 04:42:16.790
SPEAKER: At the
conclusion, a reception

04:42:16.790 --> 04:42:20.195
will follow on Kresge Oval
in the West Campus Plaza.

04:42:22.830 --> 04:42:28.575
Now, I'd like to ask the
group to stand and join

04:42:28.575 --> 04:42:31.940
the MIT chorallaries in
singing the school song.

04:42:39.732 --> 04:42:49.959
[MUSIC - MIT CHORALLARIES,
 "ARISE ALL YE OF MIT"]

04:42:49.959 --> 04:42:55.284
CHORALLARIES: (SINGING)
Arise all ye of MIT,

04:42:55.284 --> 04:42:57.410
in loyal fellowship.

04:43:00.863 --> 04:43:11.940
The future beckons unto ye,
and life is full and rich.

04:43:11.940 --> 04:43:17.440
Arise and raise
your glass on high.

04:43:17.440 --> 04:43:25.940
Tonight shall ever
be a memory that

04:43:25.940 --> 04:43:31.865
will never die for ye of MIT.

04:43:34.715 --> 04:43:46.450
Thy sons and daughters, MIT,
return from far and wide.

04:43:46.450 --> 04:43:57.698
And gather here once more to
be renourished by thy side.

04:43:57.698 --> 04:44:09.530
And as we raise our glasses high
to pledge our love for thee,

04:44:09.530 --> 04:44:18.210
we join all those of days
gone by in praise of MIT.

04:44:21.570 --> 04:44:22.070
[CHEERING]

04:44:22.070 --> 04:44:24.195
[MUSIC - MIT CHORALLARIES, "TAKE
 ME BACK TO TECH"]

04:44:24.195 --> 04:44:26.340
CHORALLARIES:
(SINGING) Oh, I wish

04:44:26.340 --> 04:44:29.895
that I were back again at Tech
on Boylston Street, dressed

04:44:29.895 --> 04:44:33.310
in my dinky uniform
so dapper and so neat.

04:44:33.310 --> 04:44:35.070
I'm crazy after calculus.

04:44:35.070 --> 04:44:36.990
I never had enough.

04:44:36.990 --> 04:44:39.570
It was hard to be
dragged away so young.

04:44:39.570 --> 04:44:41.000
It was horribly, awfully tough.

04:44:41.000 --> 04:44:45.240
Hurrah for technology,
-ology, -ology, oh.

04:44:45.240 --> 04:44:48.373
Glorious old technology,
-ology, ology, oh.

04:44:48.373 --> 04:44:51.630
Back in the days that were free
from care in the 'ology varsity

04:44:51.630 --> 04:44:55.440
shop, with nothing to do but
analyze air in an anemometrical

04:44:55.440 --> 04:44:56.400
top--

04:44:56.400 --> 04:44:59.940
the differentiation of
the trigonometric powers,

04:44:59.940 --> 04:45:01.750
the constant pi
that made me sign

04:45:01.750 --> 04:45:03.780
in those happy days of ours.

04:45:03.780 --> 04:45:07.980
Hoorah, for technology,
-ology, -ology, oh.

04:45:07.980 --> 04:45:12.156
Glorious old technology,
-ology, -ology, oh.

04:45:12.156 --> 04:45:14.946
Take me back on a special train
to the glorious Institute,

04:45:14.946 --> 04:45:17.990
I yearn for the inspiration
of a technological toot.

04:45:17.990 --> 04:45:18.970
Toot-toot.

04:45:18.970 --> 04:45:21.910
I'd shun the quizzical, physical
profs, the chapel and all that.

04:45:21.910 --> 04:45:25.830
But how I'd love to go
again on a scientific bat.

04:45:25.830 --> 04:45:28.443
La, la, la la, la, la la, la,
la la, la, la la, la, la la,

04:45:28.443 --> 04:45:30.893
la, la la, la, la la, la,
la la, la, la la, la, la la,

04:45:30.893 --> 04:45:33.425
la, la la, la, la la,
la, la la, la, la la,

04:45:33.425 --> 04:45:37.345
ta da, ta, da, ta, da, ta, da,
ta, dum, ta, dum, ta, dum, ta,

04:45:37.345 --> 04:45:38.080
dum--

04:45:38.080 --> 04:45:46.080
Oh, M-A-S-S-A-C-H-U-S-E-T-T-S
I-N-S-T-I-T-U-T-E-O-F-T-E

04:45:46.080 --> 04:45:52.360
and then, it's C-H-N-O-L-O-G
and Y, comes after G,

04:45:52.360 --> 04:45:56.600
it's the Massachusetts
Institute of Technology.

04:45:56.600 --> 04:45:57.100
Hey!

04:45:57.100 --> 04:45:58.600
[APPLAUSE]

